      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(config): config-surface reduction tranche 1 — retire dead keys, dedupe channel schemas, add growth ratchet",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `openclaw.json` surface has grown past 10,000 documented config paths (plus ~650 `OPENCLAW_*` env vars) and is growing by roughly 40 paths/day. Dead keys linger after retirement, ~20 identical messaging options are hand-copied into 7 of 9 bundled channel schemas (drifting independently — GoogleChat silently lacked knobs every other channel has), and nothing pushes back on new growth.\n\nThis PR is the first tranche of the config-surface reduction program (maintainer-directed): retire dead/aliased keys, deduplicate the channel schema layer, and add a ratchet so the surface can only grow deliberately.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nPer AGENTS.md config policy: runtime reads canonical config only; the config/env surface bar is high; prefer removing/consolidating config options when touching these surfaces.\n\n**Phase 1 — retirements (all doctor-migrated).** Removed keys whose runtime readers are gone or that alias a canonical key: root `tui`, `canvasHost`, `defaultModel`; `cron.webhook`; `commands.modelsWrite`; `messages.messagePrefix`; `tools.media.asyncCompletion`; `tools.message.allowCrossContextSend`; `talk`/Discord `realtime.voice` aliases; media Deepgram option aliases; MCP timeout aliases (`connectTimeout`/`connect_timeout`/`timeout` → canonical `connectionTimeoutMs`/`requestTimeoutMs`, seconds→ms preserved); `session.maintenance.pruneDays`; `session.resetByType.dm`; Telegram `dm.threadReplies` family; Slack `dm.replyToMode`; WhatsApp `exposeErrorText`; GoogleChat `actions.reactions`; thread-binding `spawnAcpSessions`/`spawnSubagentSessions` aliases. Every removal: schema+types+labels+help deleted, `openclaw doctor --fix` migration (move value to canonical home or strip no-ops; canonical value wins on conflict), dead-config-keys test, dated deprecation-compat record (window to 2026-09-18), docs updated. Candidates that turned out to have live readers were kept (`messages.removeAckAfterReply`, `cron.webhookToken`). Env: deprecated `OPENCLAW_DEBUG_PROXY_DB_PATH`/`_BLOB_DIR` removed; auto-update gates collapsed to documented `OPENCLAW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE`.\n\n**Phase 2 — channel schema dedup (no user-visible changes except two intentional ones).** New internal `buildCommonChannelAccountShape()` (generalizing the WhatsApp pattern) now emits the ~20 shared messaging leaves for all eight bundled channel schema families; shared builders for exec approvals, group entries, reactions, allowBots, botLoopProtection, read receipts, name-matching; channel TS types extend `CommonChannelMessagingConfig`. Intentional surface changes: (1) legacy nested `dm.{policy,allowFrom}` retired on Discord/Slack/GoogleChat (doctor promotes to canonical top-level keys); (2) GoogleChat gains the shared `dmPolicy`/`allowFrom`/`markdown`/`heartbeat`/`contextVisibility` knobs it was missing (generic runtime readers verified). All other channel baseline paths byte-equivalent before/after.\n\n**Phase 0 — growth ratchet.** `pnpm config:docs:check` now also enforces a tracked per-kind count budget (`docs/.generated/config-baseline.counts.json`). Surface growth fails the check until the budget is consciously raised in the same PR; shrinkage must be ratcheted down via `config:docs:gen`. Runs in the existing `workflow-sanity` generated-doc-baselines lane and the changed-lanes release-metadata plan.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Existing configs keep working: `openclaw doctor --fix` migrates every retired key (values move to their canonical home; no-ops are stripped with a named change message). Configs that skip doctor and still set retired keys fail validation with a message naming the replacement — consistent with the documented ~2-month migration window.\n- Plugin SDK: type-only export `TelegramDmThreadReplies` removed with its retired key (no callable surface change; `plugin-sdk:surface:check` green). One non-callable schema re-export added for the shared mention-patterns schema.\n- Config-surface delta (ClawSweeper reviewMetrics): core paths -49, channel net -20 (18 legacy nested dm paths removed, 20 GoogleChat gap-closure paths added, -22 from Phase 1 retirements), direction: shrinking. Ratchet budget initialized at core 2980 / channel 3732 / plugin 3483; budget file initialized so further growth is opt-in and reviewable.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused suites (all green): dead-config-keys, schema-regressions, channel-alias-migration, doctor legacy-config migrations + deprecation-compat, per-channel config/doctor-contract suites (Discord/Telegram/Slack/WhatsApp/Signal/iMessage/GoogleChat/IRC/Matrix/LINE), doc-baseline integration (ratchet growth/stale/write modes), MCP transport/CLI, Talk normalization, WhatsApp accounts/inbound.\n- `pnpm tsgo:core` and `pnpm tsgo:extensions:test` green; `pnpm config:docs:check`, `pnpm config:channels:check`, `pnpm plugin-sdk:surface:check` green; `git diff --check` clean.\n- Channel baseline path diff verified byte-equivalent outside the 38 intentional path changes (18 removed legacy dm paths, 20 added GoogleChat paths).\n- Fresh autoreview: clean (Phase 2 fixed two type-fidelity findings it raised; Phase 0 zero findings).\n- Hosted CI on this PR is the land gate (OPENCLAW_TESTBOX=1 scripts/pr flow).\n\n- Named tradeoff: legacy debug-proxy sidecars stored at custom `OPENCLAW_DEBUG_PROXY_DB_PATH`/`_BLOB_DIR` locations (both @deprecated, undocumented) are not auto-imported by the one-time sidecar migration; the default-path migration is unchanged. Diagnostic capture cache, per AGENTS.md cache-migration policy.\n- Autoreview: 5 rounds; fixed dangling help-test fixtures, non-positive MCP timeout migration guard, Hermes importer canonicalization; final round clean (0 findings, patch-correct 0.9).\n",
